#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0418 expect=violation domain=SE
#note "Authority: SDTM/SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0418, Rule 'TAETORD order of elements match order in TA within ARM of the Subject'. Partially Executable (Underreporting): the Check tests only membership in the study-wide TA.TAETORD set, not the subject's own arm nor the order, so this fixture keeps every row valid WITHIN the subject's arm (DM.ARMCD) and in TA order -- no row the authority flags beyond what the Check sees. The primary is SE, not TA: the rule is scope ALL and with TA as the primary a foreign-bound and a primary-bound read of TAETORD would agree. Row 6: S1-002 (arm B) records its Follow-up element with TAETORD=4; arm B (and every arm) plans Follow-up at order 3 and no arm has an order 4, so the order matches nothing in TA -> FIRES. Every other row is its element's order within the subject's own arm -> silent. ALSO THE S3 FOREIGN-DISCRIMINATION PIN (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3): TAETORD=4 exists only in the primary SE, so a port that read TAETORD from SE instead of TA would find row 6's own value in its own set and fall silent."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=6 USUBJID=S1-002 SESEQ=3 TAETORD=4
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col TAETORD type=Num  label="Planned Order of Element within Arm"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
---
S1 | SE | S1-001 | 1 | SCRN | Screening | 1 | 2024-01-01
S1 | SE | S1-001 | 2 | TRTA | Drug A    | 2 | 2024-01-10
S1 | SE | S1-001 | 3 | FU   | Follow-up | 3 | 2024-02-10
S1 | SE | S1-002 | 1 | SCRN | Screening | 1 | 2024-01-02
S1 | SE | S1-002 | 2 | TRTB | Drug B    | 2 | 2024-01-11
S1 | SE | S1-002 | 3 | FU   | Follow-up | 4 | 2024-02-11
---

dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
---
S1 | DM | S1-001 | A | Drug A
S1 | DM | S1-002 | B | Drug B
---

dataset TA label="Trial Arms"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col TAETORD type=Num  label="Planned Order of Element within Arm"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col EPOCH   type=Char label="Epoch"
---
S1 | TA | A | Drug A | 1 | SCRN | Screening | SCREENING
S1 | TA | A | Drug A | 2 | TRTA | Drug A    | TREATMENT
S1 | TA | A | Drug A | 3 | FU   | Follow-up | FOLLOW-UP
S1 | TA | B | Drug B | 1 | SCRN | Screening | SCREENING
S1 | TA | B | Drug B | 2 | TRTB | Drug B    | TREATMENT
S1 | TA | B | Drug B | 3 | FU   | Follow-up | FOLLOW-UP
---
